WEBVTT

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.660
Weaponization and delivery are often paired because one describes preparation of a harmful

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:06.880
capability and the other describes movement toward

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:08.000
the target environment.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.970
In this course, those stages stay high level and defensive.

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:15.095
The useful defender view is about reducing the chance that suspicious content reaches

00:00:15.095 --> 00:00:16.000
users or systems,

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.000
and improving the chance that attempted delivery is noticed.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.854
Email security controls, attachment handling, web filtering, application allowlisting,

00:00:22.854 --> 00:00:23.995
supplier review, safe file handling,

00:00:23.995 --> 00:00:26.000
and user reporting all matter here.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.000
So does telemetry.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.860
If a suspicious file is blocked, a user reports a message,

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:31.995
or an inbound pattern changes suddenly,

00:00:31.995 --> 00:00:35.195
the team should have enough context to investigate without guessing.

00:00:35.195 --> 00:00:37.000
Delivery is also a human and process problem.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.570
People need an easy way to report suspicious content,

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:42.490
and analysts need a reliable way to connect those reports to

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:43.975
logs and control events.

00:00:43.975 --> 00:00:46.970
The goal is not to teach how delivery works offensively.

00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:49.975
The goal is to help defenders ask whether inbound paths are governed,

00:00:49.975 --> 00:00:51.980
whether controls are producing usable evidence,

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:55.410
and whether response teams can connect a suspicious delivery signal to later system

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:56.210
behavior.

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:58.970
Delivery-focused defense should also include workflow clarity.

00:00:58.970 --> 00:01:03.000
When a user reports suspicious content, the team should know where the report goes,

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.005
how it is enriched, how similar activity is searched for,

00:01:06.005 --> 00:01:08.330
and how results are communicated back to the people who

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:09.000
need to act.
